{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ya9srVNui7uXya69VPCdnW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Root causes\n2\t\n3\tThe closed list a fix item names with a `Root-cause:` line in its spec's\n4\tproblem. `attavo spec-gate` refuses a root cause that is not listed here;\n5\tadding one is an item's deliberate act, in the same change as the fix.\n6\tSymptom counts do not converge. The number to read is the count of\n7\tdistinct root causes named by the fix items merged over the last N items:\n8\tflat while items merge is convergence; growing names the next invariant.\n9\t\n10\tRead it with: grep -h '^Root-cause:' attest/specs/*/spec.md | sort | uniq -c\n11\t\n12\t- shared-working-copy: the executor, the driver, the screen and counsel wrote into one checkout; the invariant is that while a build runs the checkout is the executor's and every other actor writes records from a detached worktree (#227; #229 build-01, build-04's marker in the gate worktree; the driver's records-only commits; tests/test_retry.py::test_counsels_verdict_routes_the_next_pass, 8 of 40 runs with passes every 0.5 s beside a committing worker (#257))\n13\t- deny-list-tool-surface: the executor's tools were removed one at a time as each one hurt; the invariant is a boundary told at the edit and a foreground long enough for one test run (#227 build-01; #229 build-01, build-05)\n14\t- dogfood-tests-told-apart-by-a-list: the tests that read this repository's own records were named in hand-copied lists instead of by their marker; the invariant is one marker and no list (#229 build-04)\n15\t- liveness-by-proxy: a stage's liveness was read from a pid and a host name written by a process that is not the holder; the invariant is a heartbeat written by the holder (#229 build-04, build-05)\n16\t- classification-by-reading-prose: a stop's class and provenance were derived by scanning the transcript for words; the invariant is that class and provenance come from structured output and gate results (#219; #229 build-01, build-03, build-04, build-05)\n17\t- tests-on-real-clocks: the product judged its bounds on the machine's own clock, so a test reached a bound only by waiting for it, and fixed loops of passes with sleeps hoped a detached worker had finished; the invariant is that every bound the product judges reads one clock, a file the tests set instead of waiting, and a test waits on a fact, never on time (#257; tests/test_retry.py's 36 s of real sleeps and the suite bound crossed at 180 s; tests/test_testtool.py::test_attavo_test_ends_a_run_past_its_bound_with_everything_it_started, PermissionError on os.killpg under load on 2026-09-28, PR #256)\n18\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85f25502-53d0-422c-981c-6aef437fba5e","uuid":"fcbcb17e-5cfe-4160-b257-588b091cd080","timestamp":"2026-09-30T02:03:02.831Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-274/attest/root-causes.md","content":"# Root causes\n\nThe closed list a fix item names with a `Root-cause:` line in its spec's\nproblem. `attavo spec-gate` refuses a root cause that is not listed here;\nadding one is an item's deliberate act, in the same change as the fix.\nSymptom counts do not converge. The number to read is the count of\ndistinct root causes named by the fix items merged over the last N items:\nflat while items merge is convergence; growing names the next invariant.\n\nRead it with: grep -h '^Root-cause:' attest/specs/*/spec.md | sort | uniq -c\n\n- shared-working-copy: the executor, the driver, the screen and counsel wrote into one checkout; the invariant is that while a build runs the checkout is the executor's and every other actor writes records from a detached worktree (#227; #229 build-01, build-04's marker in the gate worktree; the driver's records-only commits; tests/test_retry.py::test_counsels_verdict_routes_the_next_pass, 8 of 40 runs with passes every 0.5 s beside a committing worker (#257))\n- deny-list-tool-surface: the executor's tools were removed one at a time as each one hurt; the invariant is a boundary told at the edit and a foreground long enough for one test run (#227 build-01; #229 build-01, build-05)\n- dogfood-tests-told-apart-by-a-list: the tests that read this repository's own records were named in hand-copied lists instead of by their marker; the invariant is one marker and no list (#229 build-04)\n- liveness-by-proxy: a stage's liveness was read from a pid and a host name written by a process that is not the holder; the invariant is a heartbeat written by the holder (#229 build-04, build-05)\n- classification-by-reading-prose: a stop's class and provenance were derived by scanning the transcript for words; the invariant is that class and provenance come from structured output and gate results (#219; #229 build-01, build-03, build-04, build-05)\n- tests-on-real-clocks: the product judged its bounds on the machine's own clock, so a test reached a bound only by waiting for it, and fixed loops of passes with sleeps hoped a detached worker had finished; the invariant is that every bound the product judges reads one clock, a file the tests set instead of waiting, and a test waits on a fact, never on time (#257; tests/test_retry.py's 36 s of real sleeps and the suite bound crossed at 180 s; tests/test_testtool.py::test_attavo_test_ends_a_run_past_its_bound_with_everything_it_started, PermissionError on os.killpg under load on 2026-09-28, PR #256)\n","numLines":18,"startLine":1,"totalLines":18}}}
